From 9b68273594a961d34fecfdf89dbd3caaa038a3ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:28:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] provider: a plugin provider's price rate saves and prices
 (#3517)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A plugin provider's editor saved its price rate and answered success, and
the rate was still nowhere: Save keeps only the user's own fields of a
signed-in account, and the rate was not among them, so providers.json
never carried it; and withPicks, which lays those fields over the sign-in
in All and AlsoOn, didn't carry it either, so a rate set by hand in
providers.json would not have priced a call anyway — usage went out at
the maker's price, when a relay behind a plugin often bills a fraction of
it (the editor's Save was the only way to set a provider's rate).

Keep the rate with the rest of the user's own knobs: in Save's account
fields and in withPicks. A plugin provider's rate now saves, the editor
shows it again, and EffectivePrice scales the model's price by it, as a
custom provider's has always (#3517). A plugin that prices its own models
(#3038) would still be scaled by the rate, as its proposal says.

Fixes #3517

